# Development Workflow

Every feature or bugfix MUST follow this strict order:

## Step 1: Branch

- Create a branch from `main` (trunk-based development, `main` is the only long-lived branch)
- Naming: `feature/<context>-<description>`, `fix/<context>-<description>`, `improvement/<context>-<description>`, `chore/<description>`, `docs/<description>`
- Example: `feature/dispatch-smart-finder`, `fix/assignment-overlap-check`

## Step 2: Understand

- Read the relevant docs in `docs/` before coding
- Identify which module this belongs to: `auth`, `user`, `asset`, `project`, `assignment`, `maintenance`, `dashboard`, `dispatch`, `shared`, `frontend`
- Check existing code for reusable patterns — avoid redundant code

## Step 3: Test First

- Write failing tests BEFORE writing implementation code
- Domain logic: unit tests with `TestMethod_Scenario_Expected` naming
- API endpoints: integration tests with authenticated test client where practical
- Prefer table-driven tests for availability, conflict, and ranking

## Step 4: Implement

- Write the simplest code that makes the tests pass — no over-engineering
- Follow layers: Handler → Service → Repository
- Keep handlers thin; put business rules in services

## Step 5: Verify

- Backend: `golangci-lint run` + `go test ./...`
- Frontend: `npm run lint` + `npx tsc --noEmit` + `npm test` (in `frontend/`)
- No `any` type (TS), no swallowed errors (Go), no magic ranking weights without named constants

## Step 6: Commit

- Use Conventional Commits: `feat(asset):`, `fix(dispatch):`, `test(assignment):`
- Scope must match module: auth, user, asset, project, assignment, maintenance, dashboard, dispatch, shared, frontend
- Commit messages explain WHY, not WHAT

## Step 7: Push and PR

- Push to origin: `git push -u origin feature/xxx`
- Create PR targeting `main`
- PR title follows Conventional Commits format
- PR description must include: Summary, Motivation, Changes, Testing checklist
- PR must be < 900 lines of changed code — split larger changes
- Wait for CI + review; use squash merge

## Enforcement (CI)

- **PR base branch**: `.github/workflows/pr-base-check.yml` fails if PR targets any branch other than `main`
- **Lint, test, build**: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs on every PR
- **Branch naming**: Warns if branch does not match `feature/*`, `fix/*`, `improvement/*`, `chore/*`, `docs/*`

## Sync Daily

- Run `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main` daily to avoid merge conflicts
- Use `--force-with-lease` (never `--force`) when pushing after rebase
